{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787919643635,"sessionID":"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_69fa284056574b928f19594c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/src/internal/ui/app.go","offset":1270,"limit":70},"output":"<path>/workspace/src/internal/ui/app.go</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1270: \t\t// doomed pane.\n1271: \t\tif !a.detail.tigAvailable {\n1272: \t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"tig is not installed on the host — install it, or use the diff tab\")\n1273: \t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n1274: \t\t}\n1275: \t\tif a.detail.job.Branch == \"\" {\n1276: \t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"no branch known for this job\")\n1277: \t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n1278: \t\t}\n1279: \t\t// The job is passed by Name (id_slug), not ID: `mg diff` resolves the\n1280: \t\t// job's branch via an exact match on that tail segment (see launch.\n1281: \t\t// Tig's own doc), and there is no profile flag — mg diff is a host\n1282: \t\t// git command, not a session launch.\n1283: \t\tdesc, err := launch.Tig(a.detail.job.Name, a.root, a.settings.Terminal)\n1284: \t\tif err != nil {\n1285: \t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(cmdErrorText(err))\n1286: \t\t} else {\n1287: \t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"→ tig in \" + desc)\n1288: \t\t}\n1289: \t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n1290: \tcase \"l\":\n1291: \t\t// Tail the job's mg-jdi run.log in a tmux split pane / new terminal —\n1292: \t\t// a live `tail -f` of the same sidecar the log tab (key 5) reads, so a\n1293: \t\t// user can watch the currently running agent's output grow without\n1294: \t\t// pressing ctrl+r. Like \"t\" it spawns a host-side pane (see\n1295: \t\t// launch.Tail), unlike \"j\" which stays background-only. Gated on a\n1296: \t\t// run.log existing for this job — the same condition under which the\n1297: \t\t// log tab shows real content — and deliberately with no branch guard\n1298: \t\t// (unlike \"t\"/\"P\"/\"c\"/\"g\"): the log sidecar is job-name-keyed, not\n1299: \t\t// branch-keyed, so a branch-less working-tree job can tail too.\n1300: \t\tif !a.detail.runLogExists() {\n1301: \t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"no mg jdi run has happened for this job yet\")\n1302: \t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n1303: \t\t}\n1304: \t\t// The launch path takes the absolute run.log path directly — no\n1305: \t\t// mg-binary hop, no profile flag: `tail -f` is a plain host command.\n1306: \t\t// Same job.Root the gate just checked, so the two can never disagree.\n1307: \t\tdesc, err := launch.Tail(job.JDIRunLogPath(a.detail.job.Root, a.detail.job.Name), a.settings.Terminal)\n1308: \t\tif err != nil {\n1309: \t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(cmdErrorText(err))\n1310: \t\t} else {\n1311: \t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"→ tailing run.log in \" + desc)\n1312: \t\t}\n1313: \t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n1314: \tcase \"c\":\n1315: \t\t// Commit all uncommitted changes in this job's worktree — a\n1316: \t\t// catch-all sweep for the files agents sometimes leave behind, which\n1317: \t\t// would otherwise trip mg done's clean-tree check. A host-side git\n1318: \t\t// action like \"P\", not an agent launch: the commit runs in the job's\n1319: \t\t// own worktree so it lands on the job branch (see commitAllCmd).\n1320: \t\tif a.detail.job.Branch == \"\" {\n1321: \t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"no branch known for this job\")\n1322: \t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n1323: \t\t}\n1324: \t\treturn a, a.commitAllCmd()\n1325: \tcase \"g\":\n1326: \t\t// Open the git panel: the discoverable entry for the detail view's\n1327: \t\t// git commands (commit all / push to origin / merge default branch).\n1328: \t\t// \"g\" used to be the file viewer's scroll-to-top key (shared with\n1329: \t\t// \"home\"); the panel takes it over, and scroll-to-top stays\n1330: \t\t// reachable via \"home\" (see detail.go's scroll). The \"P\"/\"c\" direct\n1331: \t\t// accelerators stay bound too — the panel is the discoverable\n1332: \t\t// surface, not a removal of the old keys. Gated on the job having a\n1333: \t\t// branch like \"P\"/\"c\"/\"t\": every action in the panel targets the\n1334: \t\t// job's worktree branch.\n1335: \t\tif a.detail.job.Branch == \"\" {\n1336: \t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"no branch known for this job\")\n1337: \t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n1338: \t\t}\n1339: \t\ta.gitPanel = newGitPanelView(a.width, a.height)\n\n(Showing lines 1270-1339 of 1662. Use offset=1340 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\t\t// doomed pane.\n\t\tif !a.detail.tigAvailable {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"tig is not installed on the host — install it, or use the diff tab\")\n\t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n\t\t}\n\t\tif a.detail.job.Branch == \"\" {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"no branch known for this job\")\n\t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n\t\t}\n\t\t// The job is passed by Name (id_slug), not ID: `mg diff` resolves the\n\t\t// job's branch via an exact match on that tail segment (see launch.\n\t\t// Tig's own doc), and there is no profile flag — mg diff is a host\n\t\t// git command, not a session launch.\n\t\tdesc, err := launch.Tig(a.detail.job.Name, a.root, a.settings.Terminal)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(cmdErrorText(err))\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"→ tig in \" + desc)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/src/internal/ui/app.go","text":"\t\t// doomed pane.\n\t\tif !a.detail.tigAvailable {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"tig is not installed on the host — install it, or use the diff tab\")\n\t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n\t\t}\n\t\tif a.detail.job.Branch == \"\" {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"no branch known for this job\")\n\t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n\t\t}\n\t\t// The job is passed by Name (id_slug), not ID: `mg diff` resolves the\n\t\t// job's branch via an exact match on that tail segment (see launch.\n\t\t// Tig's own doc), and there is no profile flag — mg diff is a host\n\t\t// git command, not a session launch.\n\t\tdesc, err := launch.Tig(a.detail.job.Name, a.root, a.settings.Terminal)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(cmdErrorText(err))\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"→ tig in \" + desc)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n\tcase \"l\":\n\t\t// Tail the job's mg-jdi run.log in a tmux split pane / new terminal —\n\t\t// a live `tail -f` of the same sidecar the log tab (key 5) reads, so a\n\t\t// user can watch the currently running agent's output grow without\n\t\t// pressing ctrl+r. Like \"t\" it spawns a host-side pane (see\n\t\t// launch.Tail), unlike \"j\" which stays background-only. Gated on a\n\t\t// run.log existing for this job — the same condition under which the\n\t\t// log tab shows real content — and deliberately with no branch guard\n\t\t// (unlike \"t\"/\"P\"/\"c\"/\"g\"): the log sidecar is job-name-keyed, not\n\t\t// branch-keyed, so a branch-less working-tree job can tail too.\n\t\tif !a.detail.runLogExists() {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"no mg jdi run has happened for this job yet\")\n\t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n\t\t}\n\t\t// The launch path takes the absolute run.log path directly — no\n\t\t// mg-binary hop, no profile flag: `tail -f` is a plain host command.\n\t\t// Same job.Root the gate just checked, so the two can never disagree.\n\t\tdesc, err := launch.Tail(job.JDIRunLogPath(a.detail.job.Root, a.detail.job.Name), a.settings.Terminal)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(cmdErrorText(err))\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"→ tailing run.log in \" + desc)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n\tcase \"c\":\n\t\t// Commit all uncommitted changes in this job's worktree — a\n\t\t// catch-all sweep for the files agents sometimes leave behind, which\n\t\t// would otherwise trip mg done's clean-tree check. A host-side git\n\t\t// action like \"P\", not an agent launch: the commit runs in the job's\n\t\t// own worktree so it lands on the job branch (see commitAllCmd).\n\t\tif a.detail.job.Branch == \"\" {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"no branch known for this job\")\n\t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn a, a.commitAllCmd()\n\tcase \"g\":\n\t\t// Open the git panel: the discoverable entry for the detail view's\n\t\t// git commands (commit all / push to origin / merge default branch).\n\t\t// \"g\" used to be the file viewer's scroll-to-top key (shared with\n\t\t// \"home\"); the panel takes it over, and scroll-to-top stays\n\t\t// reachable via \"home\" (see detail.go's scroll). The \"P\"/\"c\" direct\n\t\t// accelerators stay bound too — the panel is the discoverable\n\t\t// surface, not a removal of the old keys. Gated on the job having a\n\t\t// branch like \"P\"/\"c\"/\"t\": every action in the panel targets the\n\t\t// job's worktree branch.\n\t\tif a.detail.job.Branch == \"\" {\n\t\t\ta.detail.setStatus(\"no branch known for this job\")\n\t\t\treturn a, a.armStatusExpiry()\n\t\t}\n\t\ta.gitPanel = newGitPanelView(a.width, a.height)","lineStart":1270,"lineEnd":1339,"totalLines":1662,"truncated":true}},"title":"src/internal/ui/app.go","time":{"start":1787919643628,"end":1787919643633}},"id":"prt_04850af1f0016RiA3FXzWFjqx3","sessionID":"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o","messageID":"msg_04850a6b9001mH2BmXcaLZDn0A"}}
