{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787920252390,"sessionID":"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_40b9cd540c934c959191e4a6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md","limit":40,"offset":45},"output":"<path>/workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n45: and declare a network isolation level (`network:`); both are designed but not\n46: yet enforced. `docs/agent-template.md` in the manigot checkout is a copy-me\n47: reference agent showing the full frontmatter surface and every guardrail.\n48: Every job-worktree session ends with a host-side sweep-commit of leftover\n49: changes (a `[<id>] chore: commit all` commit), so read-only agents' outputs\n50: (like the analyst's tasks.md) are committed after their session and `mg done`\n51: is never blocked by uncommitted leftovers. The sweep never runs for plain\n52: sessions, `mg host` sessions, or any `--job` resolution that stays on the main\n53: worktree — the flat-scan fallback (a repo with no local branches, or a\n54: non-git project — there is no job worktree to sweep) and a pre-worktree job\n55: (its branch still checked out in the main worktree itself) alike — since the\n56: main project root holds the user's own uncommitted work.\n57: Agent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\n58: session git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\n59: pushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\n60: The manigot TUI's job detail view also offers a `t` key that opens the job's\n61: branch diff in tig (`mg diff <job> --tig`) in a tmux split pane / new\n62: terminal, gated on tig being installed on the host, and an `l` key that\n63: tails the job's mg-jdi `run.log` live in a tmux split pane / new terminal,\n64: gated on a run.log existing for the job.\n65: `mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a read-only control\n66: API over a registry of project roots (an explicit config file,\n67: `<manigot checkout>/config/serve.json`, holding `{\"projects\": [\"/abs/root\",\n68: ...]}` — no scanning; changing it means editing and restarting), so any\n69: surface — a web UI, a native GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client\n70: from localhost or a VPS. It binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default (tokenless —\n71: the machine's own user is the trust boundary); a non-loopback bind REQUIRES a\n72: bearer token (`--token` or `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN`) or the daemon refuses to start,\n73: and TLS is the reverse proxy's job (Caddy/nginx), never the daemon's. The v1\n74: API is read-only (projects, jobs, job files, jdi status + logs, diff, agents,\n75: health) and is a new trust boundary: URL segments are never joined into\n76: filesystem paths, credentials are never returned in any response, every\n77: request is audit-logged (never the token), and mutating operations (a later\n78: job) must serialize per project root via the `serve.ProjectLocks` pattern.\n79: Copying text from inside a session uses OSC 52: your terminal emulator must\n80: support it, and tmux needs `set-clipboard on` when the session runs inside\n81: tmux (mg forwards your terminal environment into the container and warns at\n82: session start when it detects tmux would swallow the clipboard writes — see\n83: the manigot README's \"Clipboard / copying from agent sessions\" section).\n84: One deliberate exception in that forwarding: OpenCode sessions never see\n\n(Showing lines 45-84 of 124. Use offset=85 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"and declare a network isolation level (`network:`); both are designed but not\nyet enforced. `docs/agent-template.md` in the manigot checkout is a copy-me\nreference agent showing the full frontmatter surface and every guardrail.\nEvery job-worktree session ends with a host-side sweep-commit of leftover\nchanges (a `[<id>] chore: commit all` commit), so read-only agents' outputs\n(like the analyst's tasks.md) are committed after their session and `mg done`\nis never blocked by uncommitted leftovers. The sweep never runs for plain\nsessions, `mg host` sessions, or any `--job` resolution that stays on the main\nworktree — the flat-scan fallback (a repo with no local branches, or a\nnon-git project — there is no job worktree to sweep) and a pre-worktree job\n(its branch still checked out in the main worktree itself) alike — since the\nmain project root holds the user's own uncommitted work.\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\nThe manigot TUI's job detail view also offers a `t` key that opens the job's\nbranch diff in tig (`mg diff <job> --tig`) in a tmux split pane / new\nterminal, gated on tig being installed on the host, and an `l` key that\ntails the job's mg-jdi `run.log` live in a tmux split pane / new terminal,\ngated on a run.log existing for the job.","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md","text":"and declare a network isolation level (`network:`); both are designed but not\nyet enforced. `docs/agent-template.md` in the manigot checkout is a copy-me\nreference agent showing the full frontmatter surface and every guardrail.\nEvery job-worktree session ends with a host-side sweep-commit of leftover\nchanges (a `[<id>] chore: commit all` commit), so read-only agents' outputs\n(like the analyst's tasks.md) are committed after their session and `mg done`\nis never blocked by uncommitted leftovers. The sweep never runs for plain\nsessions, `mg host` sessions, or any `--job` resolution that stays on the main\nworktree — the flat-scan fallback (a repo with no local branches, or a\nnon-git project — there is no job worktree to sweep) and a pre-worktree job\n(its branch still checked out in the main worktree itself) alike — since the\nmain project root holds the user's own uncommitted work.\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\nThe manigot TUI's job detail view also offers a `t` key that opens the job's\nbranch diff in tig (`mg diff <job> --tig`) in a tmux split pane / new\nterminal, gated on tig being installed on the host, and an `l` key that\ntails the job's mg-jdi `run.log` live in a tmux split pane / new terminal,\ngated on a run.log existing for the job.\n`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a read-only control\nAPI over a registry of project roots (an explicit config file,\n`<manigot checkout>/config/serve.json`, holding `{\"projects\": [\"/abs/root\",\n...]}` — no scanning; changing it means editing and restarting), so any\nsurface — a web UI, a native GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client\nfrom localhost or a VPS. It binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default (tokenless —\nthe machine's own user is the trust boundary); a non-loopback bind REQUIRES a\nbearer token (`--token` or `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN`) or the daemon refuses to start,\nand TLS is the reverse proxy's job (Caddy/nginx), never the daemon's. The v1\nAPI is read-only (projects, jobs, job files, jdi status + logs, diff, agents,\nhealth) and is a new trust boundary: URL segments are never joined into\nfilesystem paths, credentials are never returned in any response, every\nrequest is audit-logged (never the token), and mutating operations (a later\njob) must serialize per project root via the `serve.ProjectLocks` pattern.\nCopying text from inside a session uses OSC 52: your terminal emulator must\nsupport it, and tmux needs `set-clipboard on` when the session runs inside\ntmux (mg forwards your terminal environment into the container and warns at\nsession start when it detects tmux would swallow the clipboard writes — see\nthe manigot README's \"Clipboard / copying from agent sessions\" section).\nOne deliberate exception in that forwarding: OpenCode sessions never see","lineStart":45,"lineEnd":84,"totalLines":124,"truncated":true}},"title":"project-template/docs/AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1787920252385,"end":1787920252389}},"id":"prt_04859fcc2001DFzJ01FB0q5dKf","sessionID":"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6","messageID":"msg_04859f5eb001vpd0QkpOtNDk6T"}}
