{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787920901304,"sessionID":"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_24ede3a63b61492ca3b014cd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md","newString":"The **log** tab shows `mg jdi`'s `run.log` for this job — one section per\nagent invocation, with a timestamp/agent/attempt header; the attempt number\ncounts that agent's invocations within the run (per agent, not per run), so\na bounce back to the developer shows that developer's second call as attempt\n2. It is the *event summary* (agent invoked / result / next agent invoked) —\nfor the verbose raw stream of what an agent actually did, press `l` instead\n(see below). It reads\n\"_no mg jdi run has happened for this job yet_\" until the first `mg jdi` run\nagainst it; large files are tailed, not loaded in full. Never editable.","oldString":"The **log** tab shows `mg jdi`'s `run.log` for this job — one section per\nagent invocation, with a timestamp/agent/attempt header; the attempt number\ncounts that agent's invocations within the run (per agent, not per run), so\na bounce back to the developer shows that developer's second call as attempt\n2. It reads\n\"_no mg jdi run has happened for this job yet_\" until the first `mg jdi` run\nagainst it; large files are tailed, not loaded in full. Never editable."},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -992,9 +992,11 @@\n The **log** tab shows `mg jdi`'s `run.log` for this job — one section per\n agent invocation, with a timestamp/agent/attempt header; the attempt number\n counts that agent's invocations within the run (per agent, not per run), so\n a bounce back to the developer shows that developer's second call as attempt\n-2. It reads\n+2. It is the *event summary* (agent invoked / result / next agent invoked) —\n+for the verbose raw stream of what an agent actually did, press `l` instead\n+(see below). It reads\n \"_no mg jdi run has happened for this job yet_\" until the first `mg jdi` run\n against it; large files are tailed, not loaded in full. Never editable.\n \n The **diff** tab is the TUI's representation of `mg diff <id>`: it computes\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/README.md","patch":"Index: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -992,9 +992,11 @@\n The **log** tab shows `mg jdi`'s `run.log` for this job — one section per\n agent invocation, with a timestamp/agent/attempt header; the attempt number\n counts that agent's invocations within the run (per agent, not per run), so\n a bounce back to the developer shows that developer's second call as attempt\n-2. It reads\n+2. It is the *event summary* (agent invoked / result / next agent invoked) —\n+for the verbose raw stream of what an agent actually did, press `l` instead\n+(see below). It reads\n \"_no mg jdi run has happened for this job yet_\" until the first `mg jdi` run\n against it; large files are tailed, not loaded in full. Never editable.\n \n The **diff** tab is the TUI's representation of `mg diff <id>`: it computes\n","additions":3,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1787920901301,"end":1787920901303}},"id":"prt_04863c790001bvTz9OVOF7195w","sessionID":"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6","messageID":"msg_04863c116001UpjjOPaIZb4fgW"}}
