{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787920937486,"sessionID":"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_59a681680269496baf2b02c2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/ROADMAP.md","limit":30,"offset":99},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/ROADMAP.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n99: ### 5. Event-streaming subsystem — designed against a real consumer, now in scope\n100: \n101: **Status: PARTIALLY addressed** — the writer side landed in\n102: `health_capture-non-interactive-agent-sessions`: every non-interactive\n103: invocation's raw step-level output is now streamed *live* into the job's own\n104: `session.log` during the run (and claude-pro's `--print` path emits the full\n105: stream-json event stream), superseding the README's honest \"final answer\n106: only\" limitation. The reader side has partly landed in\n107: `guest_fix-tailing`: the detail view's `l` key now tails `session.log` — a\n108: `tail -f` pane of the verbose raw stream, distinct from the log tab's\n109: `run.log` event summary. What remains open is the item's richer *in-TUI*\n110: step-level view — the TUI log tab stays on `run.log` for now; rendering\n111: `session.log` as a structured step-level view inside the TUI is a separate,\n112: later job (the `l` tail pane is the interim reader).\n113: \n114: The polling model tells you the *stage*, not what the agent is *doing*. The\n115: old fear (\"wire-format commitment\") is answered by building it against a\n116: concrete need rather than as an abstraction: the first consumer in scope is\n117: the richer step-level `run.log` (the old \"richer logging\" backlog item),\n118: replacing the README's honest \"final answer only\" limitation. Design the\n119: writer side in the agent invocation path and the reader side in the TUI for\n120: *that* consumer; the format earns its keep before anything else attaches to\n121: it. One sizing constraint to pin before the writer design: the CLIs are\n122: asymmetric in what they emit. OpenCode's `run --format json` already streams\n123: fine-grained events (`step_start` / `tool_use` / `text` / `step_finish` with\n124: per-step tokens). Claude Code's `--print` today returns a single final-result\n125: object (`--output-format json`); it *can* stream (`--output-format\n126: stream-json`: per-message events, cost only as a per-run total on the result\n127: event) but manigot does not use it yet, and that format is more version-volatile\n128: than the stable result shape. So the writer needs either a third parser branch\n\n(Showing lines 99-128 of 167. Use offset=129 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"### 5. Event-streaming subsystem — designed against a real consumer, now in scope\n\n**Status: PARTIALLY addressed** — the writer side landed in\n`health_capture-non-interactive-agent-sessions`: every non-interactive\ninvocation's raw step-level output is now streamed *live* into the job's own\n`session.log` during the run (and claude-pro's `--print` path emits the full\nstream-json event stream), superseding the README's honest \"final answer\nonly\" limitation. The reader side has partly landed in\n`guest_fix-tailing`: the detail view's `l` key now tails `session.log` — a\n`tail -f` pane of the verbose raw stream, distinct from the log tab's\n`run.log` event summary. What remains open is the item's richer *in-TUI*\nstep-level view — the TUI log tab stays on `run.log` for now; rendering\n`session.log` as a structured step-level view inside the TUI is a separate,\nlater job (the `l` tail pane is the interim reader).\n\nThe polling model tells you the *stage*, not what the agent is *doing*. The\nold fear (\"wire-format commitment\") is answered by building it against a\nconcrete need rather than as an abstraction: the first consumer in scope is\nthe richer step-level `run.log` (the old \"richer logging\" backlog item),\nreplacing the README's honest \"final answer only\" limitation. Design the","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/ROADMAP.md","text":"### 5. Event-streaming subsystem — designed against a real consumer, now in scope\n\n**Status: PARTIALLY addressed** — the writer side landed in\n`health_capture-non-interactive-agent-sessions`: every non-interactive\ninvocation's raw step-level output is now streamed *live* into the job's own\n`session.log` during the run (and claude-pro's `--print` path emits the full\nstream-json event stream), superseding the README's honest \"final answer\nonly\" limitation. The reader side has partly landed in\n`guest_fix-tailing`: the detail view's `l` key now tails `session.log` — a\n`tail -f` pane of the verbose raw stream, distinct from the log tab's\n`run.log` event summary. What remains open is the item's richer *in-TUI*\nstep-level view — the TUI log tab stays on `run.log` for now; rendering\n`session.log` as a structured step-level view inside the TUI is a separate,\nlater job (the `l` tail pane is the interim reader).\n\nThe polling model tells you the *stage*, not what the agent is *doing*. The\nold fear (\"wire-format commitment\") is answered by building it against a\nconcrete need rather than as an abstraction: the first consumer in scope is\nthe richer step-level `run.log` (the old \"richer logging\" backlog item),\nreplacing the README's honest \"final answer only\" limitation. Design the\nwriter side in the agent invocation path and the reader side in the TUI for\n*that* consumer; the format earns its keep before anything else attaches to\nit. One sizing constraint to pin before the writer design: the CLIs are\nasymmetric in what they emit. OpenCode's `run --format json` already streams\nfine-grained events (`step_start` / `tool_use` / `text` / `step_finish` with\nper-step tokens). Claude Code's `--print` today returns a single final-result\nobject (`--output-format json`); it *can* stream (`--output-format\nstream-json`: per-message events, cost only as a per-run total on the result\nevent) but manigot does not use it yet, and that format is more version-volatile\nthan the stable result shape. So the writer needs either a third parser branch","lineStart":99,"lineEnd":128,"totalLines":167,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs/ROADMAP.md","time":{"start":1787920937482,"end":1787920937484}},"id":"prt_048647103001YOhegvg36bj3We","sessionID":"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6","messageID":"msg_0486468860012WkHsz9czgMpE7"}}
