{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787921015292,"sessionID":"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_31c677c35bae40c4906d3a67","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git status --short && echo \"---\" && wc -l docs/jobs/guest_fix-tailing/session.log && tail -5 docs/jobs/guest_fix-tailing/session.log","workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"---\n91 docs/jobs/guest_fix-tailing/session.log\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1787920042023,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_048568a68001RmyXQ3EAlEWJij\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0485623a7001ELmEzvidmyOQRw\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I now have a complete picture. Let me verify my understanding of the capture path once more, then write the analysis.\\n\\n**Findings so far:**\\n- The \\\"l\\\" tail (`launch.Tail` → `tail -f`) follows `run.log` — the *same* summary file the log tab (key 5) reads. Content is identical by design → \\\"I'd get exactly what I get in the log view.\\\"\\n- `run.log` only receives writes at invocation *boundaries* (`logAgentInvoked` before, `logInvocation` after). During a long agent invocation nothing is appended → \\\"shows no stream\\\", \\\"seems buffered\\\".\\n- The raw invocation output *is* captured (whole, into a `bytes.Buffer` via `cmd.Stdout`) and persisted verbatim post-hoc to `docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log` — a different, more verbose log that already exists, but is neither live nor what the tail follows.\\n- The existing opencode `--print` path (`opencode run --format json`, JSONL) is already captured and parsed (pinned in `jdi_test.go`), so \\\"grabbing\\\" works — but nothing streams it live.\\n\\nNow writing the task breakdown into `tasks.md`.\\n\\n\",\"time\":{\"start\":1787920026217,\"end\":1787920042019}}}\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1787920042038,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_04856c82f0013XIO7JgLO0F8AP\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0485623a7001ELmEzvidmyOQRw\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":134308,\"input\":1383,\"output\":4157,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":128768}},\"cost\":0.003949256}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1787920043226,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_04856ccd7001CdK0ostfK2qIr1\",\"messageID\":\"msg_04856c835001yBeE2PtLxMxWQu\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1787920050152,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_04856cfb0001drPTfs3h2cOLum\",\"messageID\":\"msg_04856c835001yBeE2PtLxMxWQu\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. I've analyzed the job and written the task breakdown to `tasks.md`.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Branch verified:** `fix/guest_fix-tailing` (matches the brief).\\n\\n**Root cause of the reported bug** (confirmed by reading the code, not guessing):\\n\\n1. **\\\"No stream / buffered / same as the log view\\\"** — the `l` key runs `tail -f` on `.manigot/jdi-status/<job>/run.log` (`app.go:1307` → `launch.Tail`), which is the *exact same file* the log tab (key 5) renders (`detail.go:205`). `run.log` only grows at invocation boundaries (`logAgentInvoked` before, `logInvocation` after — `jdi.go`/`jdioutput.go`), and the invocation's raw output is captured whole into a `bytes.Buffer` and only flushed post-hoc. So the tail shows the same sectioned summary, with nothing live during a long agent call.\\n\\n2. **\\\"Are we grabbing the output?\\\"** — Yes, it *is* captured (full stdout of the `--print` docker invocation) and already persisted verbatim to a different, more verbose log: `docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log` (post-hoc, per invocation). The opencode `--format json` JSONL path is already captured and pinned by existing tests. What's missing: the tail doesn't follow it, and it isn't written live.\\n\\n3. **The log-vs-tail distinction** maps cleanly onto what already exists: log tab = `run.log` event summary; tail should = the verbose raw stream (`session.log`).\\n\\n**Tasks produced (4):**\\n\\n| Task | Description | Risk |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| TASK-1 | Verify the capture path end-to-end (opencode included) + pin with a test — answers \\\"are we grabbing the output\\\" | low |\\n| TASK-2 | Stream raw output **live** into the job's `session.log` (header before, tee during the invocation), replacing post-hoc `appendSessionLog` | medium |\\n| TASK-3 | Point the `l` tail at `session.log` instead of `run.log` (gate, footer hint, status text); log tab stays on `run.log` | low-medium |\\n| TASK-4 | Update docs (`docs/AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, project-template, ROADMAP) to the new log-vs-tail description | low |\\n\\n**Key scoping decision (flagged in the analysis):** `session.log` stays in the job's folder — the prior capture job deliberately put it there (sweep-commit, `mg done` archive-carry, `mg delete`, and the serve `/jdi` endpoint all depend on that location). Only the write timing changes. Moving it to the sidecar dir is rejected because `mg done`'s `RemoveJDIStatus` would delete it on archive — that would be scope creep.\\n\\nOne open question left for the developer (in TASK-1): whether the CLIs inside the container flush stdout per event when writing to a pipe — the host-side tee will stream whatever chunks docker forwards; likely per-event for opencode, but worth confirming.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1787920043952,\"end\":1787920050150}}}\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1787920050166,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_04856e7ec001dXr044i0Y93qeu\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_04856c835001yBeE2PtLxMxWQu\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\