"kitty\\\") is invoked directly — see buildOverrideCmd. It applies\\n16: //     only when the TUI is NOT inside tmux (or tmux is not available there);\\n17: //     inside tmux the split pane above wins.\\n18: //  3. macOS Terminal.app via osascript.\\n19: //  4. A Linux terminal emulator, tried in order: gnome-terminal, ptyxis\\n20: //     (Fedora's default GNOME terminal since Fedora 41), x-terminal-emulator\\n21: //     (Debian), konsole, xterm.\\n22: //\\n23: // The command opened is always `<mg-binary> --agent <agent> --job <jobID>` run\\n24: // from the project root, matching the session launcher's invocation contract.\\n25: // <mg-binary> is the running binary's own path (os.Executable) ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n23: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1787919598374,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_01_ET_HXTmKASwqEeMVRzlzQvp3112\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/src/internal/job/jdistatus.go\"},\"output\":\"<path>/workspace/src/internal/job/jdistatus.go</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: package job\\n2: \\n3: import (\\n4: \\t\\\"encoding/json\\\"\\n5: \\t\\\"io\\\"\\n6: \\t\\\"os\\\"\\n7: \\t\\\"path/filepath\\\"\\n8: \\t\\\"strings\\\"\\n9: \\t\\\"time\\\"\\n10: )\\n11: \\n12: // ManigotRelDir is manigot's own directory inside a target project, relative\\n13: // to the project root: the home for host-side tooling state that is not job\\n14: // content and does not belong in docs/. .manigot/manigot.json holds the\\n15: // committable project settings (see the project package); .manigot/jdi-status/\\n16: // holds mg-jdi's ephemeral run state (gitignored, see .gitignore).\\n17: const ManigotRelDir = \\\".manigot\\\"\\n18: \\n19: // JDISidecarDirName is the sidecar directory mg-jdi writes its per-job\\n20: // status and run log into, under ManigotRelDir — deliberately outside any job's own directory\\n21: // (docs/jobs/<name>/) so it can never be swept into an agent's own\\n22: // `git add -A`, and gitignored entirely (see .gitignore).\\n23: const JDISidecarDirName = \\\"jdi-status\\\"\\n24: \\n25: // jdiStatusFileName / jdiRunLogFileName are the two files living under each\\n26: // job's JDIStatusDir.\\n27: const (\\n28: \\tjdiStatusFileName = \\\"status\\\"\\n29: \\tjdiRunLogFileName = \\\"run.log\\\"\\n30: )\\n31: \\n32: // JDIState is mg-jdi's reported run state for a job, read from its status\\n33: // sidecar file.\\n34: type JDIState string\\n35: \\n36: const (\\n37: \\t// JDIRunning means mg-jdi is (or, absent a fresher update, very\\n38: \\t// recently was) actively driving this job.\\n39: \\tJDIRunning JDIState = \\\"running\\\"\\n40: \\t// JDIStoppedFinished means mg-jdi's last run ended because the job's\\n41: \\t// verdict was APPROVED.\\n42: \\tJDIStoppedFinished JDIState = \\\"... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n24: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1787919598477,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_048500387001rzMaMQbhqEITzP\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0484ffc03001UObwaP6Ap88UZ0\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":47786,\"input\":331,\"output\":95,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":47360}},\"cost\":0.00046704}}\n25: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1787919599698,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_048500850001YNQiGGKZxNzXm6\",\"messageID\":\"msg_04850038c001E9SN53c7iLxDmj\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n26: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1787919601473,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_00_kVNzKaiREzcCDFcA7nu80791\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/src/internal/orchestrate/orchestrate.go\"},\"output\":\"<path>/workspace/src/internal/orchestrate/orchestrate.go</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: // Package orchestrate decides which agent mg-jdi should run next for a job,\\n2: // or whether it should stop — the agent-sequence orchestration logic.\\n3: //\\n4: // Next is a pure function of state already visible on disk/in git: a job's\\n5: // job.Stage(), how many verdict commits exist on its branch\\n6: // (git.CountVerdictCommits), and whether the branch tip is itself one of\\n7: // those verdict commits (git.LatestCommitIsVerdict). No new state file is\\n8: // needed, and mg-jdi never has to trust in-memory state across loop\\n9: // iterations — every decision re-derives cleanly from what's already\\n10: // committed, so re-running mg-jdi against the same job after it was killed\\n11: // mid-loop is always safe.\\n12: package orchestrate\\n13: \\n14: import (\\n15: \\t\\\"github.com/lmuskalla/manigot/internal/agents\\\"\\n16: \\t\\\"github.com/lmuskalla/manigot/internal/job\\\"\\n17: )\\n18: \\n19: // Kind is what mg-jdi should do next.\\n20: type Kind int\\n21: \\n22: const (\\n23: \\t// RunAgent means launch the agent named in Decision.Agent next.\\n24: \\tRunAgent Kind = iota\\n25: \\t// StopFinished means the job's verdict is APPROVED — mg-jdi's work is\\n26: \\t// done (it does not auto-merge; see the brief's completion criteria).\\n27: \\tStopFinished\\n28: \\t// StopNeedsHuman means mg-jdi cannot safely continue unattended and\\n29: \\t// must hand control back to a human.\\n30: \\tStopNeedsHuman\\n31: )\\n32: \\n33: func (k Kind) String() string {\\n34: \\tswitch k {\\n35: \\tcase RunAgent:\\n36: \\t\\treturn \\\"run-agent\\\"\\n37: \\tcase StopFinished:\\n38: \\t\\treturn \\\"stop-finished\\\"\\n39: \\tcase StopNeedsHuman:\\n40: \\t\\treturn \\\"st... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n27: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1787919601522,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"glob\",\"callID