\\":1383,\\\"output\\\":4157,\\\"reasoning\\\":0,\\\"cache\\\":{\\\"write\\\":0,\\\"read\\\":128768}},\\\"cost\\\":0.003949256}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_start\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1787920043226,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_04856ccd7001CdK0ostfK2qIr1\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_04856c835001yBeE2PtLxMxWQu\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-start\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1787920050152,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_04856cfb0001drPTfs3h2cOLum\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_04856c835001yBeE2PtLxMxWQu\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Done. I've analyzed the job and written the task breakdown to `tasks.md`.\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n**Branch verified:** `fix/guest_fix-tailing` (matches the brief).\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause of the reported bug** (confirmed by reading the code, not guessing):\\\\n\\\\n1. **\\\\\\\"No stream / buffered / same as the log view\\\\\\\"** — the `l` key runs `tail -f` on `.manigot/jdi-status/<job>/run.log` (`app.go:1307` → `launch.Tail`), which is the *exact same file* the log tab (key 5) renders (`detail.go:205`). `run.log` only grows at invocation boundaries (`logAgentInvoked` before, `logInvocation` after — `jdi.go`/`jdioutput.go`), and the invocation's raw output is captured whole into a `bytes.Buffer` and only flushed post-hoc. So the tail shows the same sectioned summary, with nothing live during a long agent call.\\\\n\\\\n2. **\\\\\\\"Are we grabbing the output?\\\\\\\"** — Yes, it *is* captured (full stdout of the `--print` docker invocation) and already persisted verbatim to a different, more verbose log: `docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log` (post-hoc, per invocation). The opencode `--format json` JSONL path is already captured and pinned by existing tests. What's missing: the tail doesn't follow it, and it isn't written live.\\\\n\\\\n3. **The log-vs-tail distinction** maps cleanly onto what already exists: log tab = `run.log` event summary; tail should = the verbose raw stream (`session.log`).\\\\n\\\\n**Tasks produced (4):**\\\\n\\\\n| Task | Description | Risk |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| TASK-1 | Verify the capture path end-to-end (opencode included) + pin with a test — answers \\\\\\\"are we grabbing the output\\\\\\\" | low |\\\\n| TASK-2 | Stream raw output **live** into the job's `session.log` (header before, tee during the invocation), replacing post-hoc `appendSessionLog` | medium |\\\\n| TASK-3 | Point the `l` tail at `session.log` instead of `run.log` (gate, footer hint, status text); log tab stays on `run.log` | low-medium |\\\\n| TASK-4 | Update docs (`docs/AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, project-template, ROADMAP) to the new log-vs-tail description | low |\\\\n\\\\n**Key scoping decision (flagged in the analysis):** `session.log` stays in the job's folder — the prior capture job deliberately put it there (sweep-commit, `mg done` archive-carry, `mg delete`, and the serve `/jdi` endpoint all depend on that location). Only the write timing changes. Moving it to the sidecar dir is rejected because `mg done`'s `RemoveJDIStatus` would delete it on archive — that would be scope creep.\\\\n\\\\nOne open question left for the developer (in TASK-1): whether the CLIs inside the container flush stdout per event when writing to a pipe — the host-side tee will stream whatever chunks docker forwards; likely per-event for opencode, but worth confirming.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1787920043952,\\\"end\\\":1787920050150}}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_finish\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1787920050166,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_04856e7ec001dXr044i0Y93qeu\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"stop\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_04856c835001yBeE2PtLxMxWQu\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_fb7b04d47ffelTPa5RFrjm6f8o\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-finish\\\",\\\"tokens\\\":{\\\"total\\\":135098,\\\"input\\\":1715,\\\"output\\\":775,\\\"reasoning\\\":0,\\\"cache\\\":{\\\"write\\\":0,\\\"read\\\":132608}},\\\"cost\\\":0.001817056}}\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"git status --short && echo \\\"---\\\" && wc -l docs/jobs/guest_fix-tailing/session.log && tail -5 docs/jobs/guest_fix-tailing/session.log\",\"time\":{\"start\":1787921015289,\"end\":1787921015291}},\"id\":\"prt_048659f7a001lC2lMB4jIvcX4j\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"messageID\":\"msg_048657dd8001OukYjOdDpK4RqM\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1787921015309,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_048659ea0001oT3X51GCv5i0Kw\",\"messageID\":\"msg_048657dd8001OukYjOdDpK4RqM\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The implementation looks coherent. Let me check the worktree state and verify the session.log handling:\",\"time\":{\"start\":1787921014432,\"end\":1787921015308}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1787921015324,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_04865a215001kuL97ylqIRX1VZ\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_048657dd8001OukYjOdDpK4RqM\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":226973,\"input\":2116,\"output\":601,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":224256}},\"cost\":0.002431972}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1787921016764,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_04865a7ba001qEOzhmJSpHHUGA\",\"messageID\":\"msg_04865a21b001Wa6aDhzFEQKDcW\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1787921018778,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_c9a6010b4aff4fd5afcfa5bd\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go\",\"limit\":110,\"offset\":280},\"output\":\"<path>/workspace/src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n280: \\t\\ttext += \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n281: \\t}\\n282: \\tfmt.Fprint(w, text)\\n283: }\\n284: \\n285: // openSessionLog opens the job's session.log for live appending and writes\\n286: // the section header for the invocation about to start — a blank-line\\n287: // separator (skipped for the very first section ever written to a fresh\\n288: // file) plus the \\\"=== <RFC3339 timestamp> <agent> (attempt N) ===\\\" header,\\n289: // the same sectioned shape appendSessionLog used to write post-hoc. The\\n290: // returned *sessionLog is the writer the invocation's raw bytes are tee'd\\n291: // into as they arrive (see commandAgentRunner.Run's io.MultiWriter), so the\\n292: // verbose log grows live during the run instead of only after it finishes —\\n293: // the whole point of the tailing fix. Callers Close it after the invocation\\n294: // so the trailing-newline guarantee holds.\\n295: func openSessionLog(path, agent string, attempt int) (*sessionLog, error) {\\n296: \\tf, err := os.OpenFile(path, os.O_CREATE|os.O_APPEND|os.O_WRONLY, 0o644)\\n297: \\tif err != nil {\\n298: \\t\\treturn nil, err\\n299: \\t}\\n300: \\n301: \\t// Blank-line separator between sections — the very first section ever\\n302: \\t// written to a fresh file starts at the top instead.\\n303: \\tif st, err := f.Stat(); err != nil {\\n304: \\t\\tf.Close()\\n305: \\t\\treturn nil, err\\n306: \\t} else if st.Size() > 0 {\\n307: \\t\\tif _, err := io.WriteString(f, \\\"\\\\n\\\"); err != nil {\\n308: \\t\\t\\tf.Close()\\n309: \\t\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n310: \\t\\t}\\n311: \\t}\\n312: \\n313: \\tif _, err := fmt.Fprintf(f, \\\"=== %s %s (attempt %d) ===\\\\n\\\", time.Now().Format(time.RFC3339), agent, attempt); err != nil {\\n314: \\t\\tf.Close()\\n315: \\t\\treturn nil, err\\n316: \\t}\\n317: \\treturn &sessionLog{f: f}, nil\\n318: }\\n319: \\n320: // sessionLog is the live, per-invocation writer behind the job's session.log\\n321: // (docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log): it owns the open file handle and\\n322: // tracks the last byte written through it, so Close can guarantee the\\n323: // section ends with a newline — the same trailing-newline guarantee\\n324: // appendSessionLog used to make post-hoc, without needing to read the file\\n325: // back. The file is opened in append mode, so concurrent appends (a second\\n326: // mg-jdi run against the same job, or the next invocation's own section)\\n327: // can never overwrite this section.\\n328: type sessionLog struct {\\n329: \\tf        *os.File\\n330: \\tlastByte byte // last byte written through this writer; 0 when nothing was written\\n331: }\\n332: \\n333: // Write appends p to the underlying file and records the last byte, so Close\\n334: // knows whether a trailing newline is still needed.\\n335: func (s *sessionLog) Write(p []byte) (int, error) {\\n336: \\tif len(p) > 0 {\\n337: \\t\\ts.lastByte = p[len(p)-1]\\n338: \\t}\\n339: \\treturn s.f.Write(p)\\n340: }\\n341: \\n342: // Close finishes the section and closes the file: a trailing newline is\\n343: // written when the last write didn't already end with one, so the next\\n344: // section's header never glues to this section's raw output. Nothing written\\n345: // at all (an invocation that produced no output) leaves the header's own\\n346: // trailing newline as the section end.\\n347: func (s *sessionLog) Close() error {\\n348: \\tif s.lastByte != 0 && s.lastByte != '\\\\n' {\\n349: \\t\\tif _, err := s.f.Write([]byte(\\\"\\\\n\\\")); err != nil {\\n350: \\t\\t\\ts.f.Close()\\n351: \\t\\t\\treturn err\\n352: \\t\\t}\\n353: \\t}\\n354: \\treturn s.f.Close()\\n355: }\\n356: \\n357: // ensureSessionLogFile creates the job's session.log if it doesn't exist yet\\n358: // (an empty file is fine — the per-invocation openSessionLog appends the\\n359: // first section header on demand), so the TUI's \\\"l\\\" tail gate — the file's\\n360: // existence — is stable from the moment an mg-jdi run begins, mirroring\\n361: // run.log's own up-front creation in openRunLog. Best-effort: a failure only\\n362: // warns; the loop still creates the file per invocation.\\n363: func ensureSessionLogFile(path string) error {\\n364: \\tf, err := os.OpenFile(path, os.O_CREATE|os.O_APPEND|os.O_WRONLY, 0o644)\\n365: \\tif err != nil {\\n366: \\t\\treturn err\\n367: \\t}\\n368: \\treturn f.Close()\\n369: }\\n370: \\n371: // logImmediateStop writes an \\\"immediate stop\\\" note to w — orchestrate.Next\\n372: // returning a Stop* decision before any agent has ever been invoked (e.g.\\n373: // job.StageDefine with an unwritten brief.md), the one case logInvocation\\n374: // never runs for. Without this, run.log would be left at 0 bytes for that\\n375: // stop, itself confusing\\n376: // independent of whether the stop was the correct call. Mirrors\\n377: // logInvocation's \\\"=== ... ===\\\" header shape so both look consistent in the\\n378: // same log, but names the stop instead of an agent/attempt.\\n379: func logImmediateStop(w io.Writer, reason string) {\\n380: \\tfmt.Fprintf(w, \\\"=== %s mg jdi stopped before running any agent ===\\\\n\\\", time.Now().Format(time.RFC3339))\\n381: \\tfmt.Fprintln(w, reason)\\n382: }\\n\\n(End of file - total 382 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"\\t\\ttext += \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n\\t}\\n\\tfmt.Fprint(w, text)\\n}\\n\\n// openSessionLog opens the job's session.log for live appending and writes\\n// the section header for the invocation about to start — a blank-line\\n// separator (skipped for the very first section ever written to a fresh\\n// file) plus the \\\"=== <RFC3339 timestamp> <agent> (attempt N) ===\\\" header,\\n// the same sectioned shape appendSessionLog used to write post-hoc. The\\n// returned *sessionLog is the writer the invocation's raw bytes are tee'd\\n// into as they arrive (see commandAgentRunner.Run's io.MultiWriter), so the\\n// verbose log grows live during the run instead of only after it finishes —\\n// the whole point of the tailing fix. Callers Close it after the invocation\\n// so the trailing-newline guarantee holds.\\nfunc openSessionLog(path, agent string, attempt int) (*sessionLog, error) {\\n\\tf, err := os.OpenFile(path, os.O_CREATE|os.O_APPEND|os.O_WRONLY, 0o644)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t}\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[],\"display\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"path\":\"/workspace/src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go\",\"text\":\"\\t\\ttext += \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n\\t}\\n\\tfmt.Fprint(w, text)\\n}\\n\\n// openSessionLog opens the job's session.log for live appending and writes\\n// the section header for the invocation about to start — a blank-line\\n// separator (skipped for the very first section ever written to a fresh\\n// file) plus the \\\"=== <RFC3339 timestamp> <agent> (attempt N) ===\\\" header,\\n// the same sectioned shape appendSessionLog used to write post-hoc. The\\n// returned *sessionLog is the writer the invocation's raw bytes are tee'd\\n// into as they arrive (see commandAgentRunner.Run's io.MultiWriter), so the\\n// verbose log grows live during the run instead of only after it finishes —\\n// the whole point of the tailing fix. Callers Close it after the invocation\\n// so the trailing-newline guarantee holds.\\nfunc openSessionLog(path, agent string, attempt int) (*sessionLog, error) {\\n\\tf, err := os.OpenFile(path, os.O_CREATE|os.O_APPEND|os.O_WRONLY, 0o644)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Blank-line separator between sections — the very first section ever\\n\\t// written to a fresh file starts at the top instead.\\n\\tif st, err := f.Stat(); err != nil {\\n\\t\\tf.Close()\\n\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t} else if st.Size() > 0 {\\n\\t\\tif _, err := io.WriteString(f, \\\"\\\\n\\\"); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tf.Close()\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tif _, err := fmt.Fprintf(f, \\\"=== %s %s (attempt %d) ===\\\\n\\\", time.Now().Format(time.RFC3339), agent, attempt); err != nil {\\n\\t\\tf.Close()\\n\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn &sessionLog{f: f}, nil\\n}\\n\\n// sessionLog is the live, per-invocation writer behind the job's session.log\\n// (docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log): it owns the open file handle and\\n// tracks the last byte written through it, so Close can guarantee the\\n// section ends with a newline — the same trailing-newline guarantee\\n// appendSessionLog used to make post-hoc, without needing to read the file\\n// back. The file is opened in append mode, so concurrent appends (a second\\n// mg-jdi run against the same job, or the next invocation's own section)\\n// can never overwrite this section.\\ntype sessionLog struct {\\n\\tf        *os.File\\n\\tlastByte byte // last byte written through this writer; 0 when nothing was written\\n}\\n\\n// Write appends p to the underlying file and records the last byte, so Close\\n// knows whether a trailing newline is still needed.\\nfunc (s *sessionLog) Write(p []byte) (int, error) {\\n\\tif len(p) > 0 {\\n\\t\\ts.lastByte = p[len(p)-1]\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn s.f.Write(p)\\n}\\n\\n// Close finishes the section and closes the file: a trailing newline is\\n// written when the last write didn't already end with one, so the next\\n// section's header never glues to this section's raw output. Nothing written\\n// at all (an invocation that produced no output) leaves the header's own\\n// trailing newline as the section end.\\nfunc (s *sessionLog) Close() error {\\n\\tif s.lastByte != 0 && s.lastByte != '\\\\n' {\\n\\t\\tif _, err := s.f.Write([]byte(\\\"\\\\n\\\")); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\ts.f.Close()\\n\\t\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn s.f.Close()\\n}\\n\\n// ensureSessionLogFile creates the job's session.log if it doesn't exist yet\\n// (an empty file is fine — the per-invocation openSessionLog appends the\\n// first section header on demand), so the TUI's \\\"l\\\" tail gate — the file's\\n// existence — is stable from the moment an mg-jdi run begins, mirroring\\n// run.log's own up-front creation in openRunLog. Best-effort: a failure only\\n// warns; the loop still creates the file per invocation.\\nfunc ensureSessionLogFile(path string) error {\\n\\tf, err := os.OpenFile(path, os.O_CREATE|os.O_APPEND|os.O_WRONLY, 0o644)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn f.Close()\\n}\\n\\n// logImmediateStop writes an \\\"immediate stop\\\" note to w — orchestrate.Next\\n// returning a Stop* decision before any agent has ever been invoked (e.g.\\n// job.StageDefine with an unwritten brief.md), the one case logInvocation\\n// never runs for. Without this, run.log would be left at 0 bytes for that\\n// stop, itself confusing\\n// independent of whether the stop was the correct call. Mirrors\\n// logInvocation's \\\"=== ... ===\\\" header shape so both look consistent in the\\n// same log, but names the stop instead of an agent/attempt.\\nfunc logImmediateStop(w io.Writer, reason string) {\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(w, \\\"=== %s mg jdi stopped before running any agent ===\\\\n\\\", time.Now().Format(time.RFC3339))\\n\\tfmt.Fprintln(w, reason)\\n}\",\"lineStart\":280,\"lineEnd\":382,\"totalLines\":382,\"truncated\":false}},\"title\":\"src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go\",\"time\":{\"start\":1787921018773,\"end\":1787921018776}},\"id\":\"prt_04865ae71001zHdy5jjCSf7SHV\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"messageID\":\"msg_04865a21b001Wa6aDhzFEQKDcW\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1787921018850,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_04865adfc001a6s14RDqgv2UC6\",\"messageID\":\"msg_04865a21b001Wa6aDhzFEQKDcW\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The worktree is clean. Let me do a final review of jdioutput.go, then write implementation.md:\",\"time\":{\"start\":1787921018364,\"end\":1787921018848}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1787921018861,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_04865afe6001VPy1aMQbCdXKgm\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_04865a21b001Wa6aDhzFEQKDcW\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":228953,\"input\":1904,\"output\":233,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":226816}},\"cost\":0.002160372}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1787921020099,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_04865b4c1001KXA7K6PSR3Q5xE\",\"messageID\":\"msg_04865afed001RxkYEIe17yszRV\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1787921038286,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"write\",\"callID\":\"call_d95013351bca472a86d01973\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"content\":\"# Implementation: Fix tailing\\n\\nid: guest\\nstatus: open\\ndeveloper: developer\\ndate: 2026-08-28\\n\\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFixed the job detail view's tail feature (\\\"l\\\" key) so it actually shows a\\nlive stream instead of duplicating the log tab. Root cause, confirmed by\\nreading the code: the tail was a `tail -f` of the mg-jdi sidecar `run.log` —\\nthe exact same file the log tab (key 5) renders — and `run.log` only grows at\\ninvocation boundaries (agent invoked / result / next agent invoked), so there\\nwas never anything live to follow. The raw step-level output *was* being\\ncaptured (full `--print` stdout) but only persisted post-hoc per invocation.\\n\\nThe fix makes the log-vs-tail distinction real: the log tab stays on\\n`run.log` (the event summary); the \\\"l\\\" tail now follows the job's own\\n`session.log` (`docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log`), which mg-jdi now streams\\ninto **live during each invocation** — section header (agent, attempt,\\ntimestamp) written before the invocation, raw bytes tee'd in as they arrive,\\ntrailing newline guaranteed on close. `session.log` stays in the job's folder\\n(unchanged location), so the sweep-commit, `mg done` archive-carry,\\n`mg delete`, and the serve `/jdi` endpoint all keep working untouched.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nTASK-1: Verified the invocation-output capture end to end and pinned it.\\n  Reading `DockerInvocation.Run` (internal/session/docker.go): `cmd.Stdout =\\n  stdout` — when the writer is a non-`*os.File` (mg-jdi's `bytes.Buffer`),\\n  exec.Cmd pipes the child's stdout and forwards every chunk to the writer:\\n  no bytes dropped, order preserved; the granularity a tail sees is whatever\\n  the in-container CLI flushes per write (docker forwards as it arrives;\\n  opencode's Go CLI writes JSONL events straight to the unbuffered pipe).\\n  Added `TestDockerInvocationRunCapturesFullStdout`,\\n  `TestDockerInvocationRunPreservesMissingTrailingNewline` and\\n  `TestDockerInvocationRunCapturesStdoutOnNonZeroExit` in\\n  src/internal/session/docker_test.go (fake `docker` emitting an opencode\\n  JSONL stream; byte-exact capture, including on a non-zero exit — failed\\n  invocations' output survives too), and extended\\n  `TestRunStopsOnNeedsHumanMarkerInOpenCodeJSONL` in src/cmd/mg/jdi_test.go\\n  to assert the raw JSONL lands verbatim in the job's `session.log`.\\n\\nTASK-2: Made mg-jdi stream each invocation's raw output live into the job's\\n  `session.log`, replacing the post-hoc `appendSessionLog` call.\\n  - src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go: `appendSessionLog` replaced by `openSessionLog`\\n    (opens the file, writes the blank-line separator + section header BEFORE\\n    the invocation) + a `sessionLog` writer type (tracks the last byte\\n    written; `Close` guarantees the section ends with a newline) +\\n    `ensureSessionLogFile` (creates the file at run start so the TUI tail\\n    gate is stable from the moment a run begins, mirroring `run.log`).\\n  - src/cmd/mg/jdi.go: `AgentRunner.Run` now takes a `live io.Writer`;\\n    `commandAgentRunner.Run` tees the container's stdout via\\n    `io.MultiWriter(&stdout, live)`; Run's loop opens the session-log\\n    section before each invocation, passes it as the live writer, and closes\\n    it after (degrading to `io.Discard` + a warning when the open fails).\\n    The loop-exit sweep comment was updated: the per-invocation sweep now\\n    runs *after* the live session.log writes and commits each section as it\\n    goes; the loop-exit sweep remains the backstop for a container that\\n    never started or a test fake that sweeps nothing.\\n  - Tests adapted: fake/err runners take the live writer (the fake tees its\\n    output into it, mirroring the real tee);\\n    `TestRunWritesSessionLogPerInvocation` updated, new\\n    `TestRunWritesSessionLogHeaderBeforeInvocation` pins the\\n    header-before-invocation contract; the `appendSessionLog` unit tests\\n    became `openSessionLog`/`sessionLog` tests (jdioutput_test.go).\\n\\nTASK-3: Pointed the detail view's \\\"l\\\" tail at the job's `session.log`.\\n  - src/internal/ui/app.go: the \\\"l\\\" case now gates on\\n    `detail.sessionLogExists()` and launches\\n    `tail -f <job.Dir>/session.log` (was `job.JDIRunLogPath(...)`); status\\n    text \\\"→ tailing session.log in ...\\\"; comments updated to the\\n    log-vs-tail distinction.\\n  - src/internal/ui/detail.go: `runLogExists` renamed to `sessionLogExists`\\n    (stat of `<job.Dir>/session.log`); the renderFooter \\\"l tail\\\" hint uses\\n    the new gate.\\n  - src/internal/ui/tail_test.go: all three tests updated to the\\n    session.log gate/path/status.\\n  - The log tab (key 5) stays on `run.log` unchanged — this is what makes\\n    the log-vs-tail difference real.\\n\\nTASK-4: Updated the documentation to the new log-vs-tail description:\\n  docs/AGENTS.md (the \\\"l\\\" key paragraph), README.md (\\\"Watching a run\\\", the\\n  `l` keybinding row, the log-tab description, and the \\\"Live tail pane\\\"\\n  section), project-template/docs/AGENTS.md (kept in sync per the hard\\n  rules), and docs/ROADMAP.md (item 5's \\\"reader side remains open\\\" note:\\n  the tail reader side has landed; the richer in-TUI structured step-level\\n  view remains open). Also synced the stale `appendSessionLog` reference in\\n  scripts/entrypoint.sh's comment (now `openSessionLog`).\\n\\n## Known issues / follow-ups\\n\\n- Intermediate agent commits inside the container may capture a\\n  partially-written session.log section (the live tee means the file grows\\n  during the run, and the in-container agent's own `git add -A` can stage\\n  it mid-write). The final file content is always complete — the host-side\\n  per-invocation sweep commits the rest — so this is cosmetic only (a\\n  partial section snapshot in an intermediate commit), not data loss.\\n- The observed streaming granularity depends on the in-container CLI's\\n  flushing (per-event for opencode's JSONL writes to a pipe; any\\n  CLI-internal buffering would deliver bursts rather than drops). A live\\n  opencode run was not available in this environment to measure actual\\n  per-event flush timing; the capture path is pinned byte-exact by tests.\\n- The serve `/jdi` endpoint and the ROADMAP's richer in-TUI step-level view\\n  remain as documented — out of scope here.\",\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/guest_fix-tailing/implementation.md\"},\"output\":\"Wrote file successfully.\",\"metadata\":{\"diagnostics\":{},\"filepath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/guest_fix-tailing/implementation.md\",\"exists\":true,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"docs/jobs/guest_fix-tailing/implementation.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1787921038281,\"end\":1787921038285}},\"id\":\"prt_04865b7cd001cHyaHQ8nOixWQq\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7a913aeffe0rISXrjcCChio6\",\"messageID\":\"msg_04865afed001Rxk