{"type":"text","timestamp":1787921809276,"sessionID":"ses_fb7999c4fffe1anLtOEgzjXUGJ","part":{"id":"prt_04871a4610017NsEpQhusGL4JD","messageID":"msg_048719c86001Iw1MR327p0gI0V","sessionID":"ses_fb7999c4fffe1anLtOEgzjXUGJ","type":"text","text":"Verdict written and committed (`3b0006b [guest] verdict: approve the tailing fix`). The remaining `M session.log` is my own session's live-streamed output — the host-side session-end sweep commits it, per design.\n\n## Review summary\n\n**Verdict: APPROVED** — all four tasks PASS.\n\n**What I verified:**\n\n- **Branch/base:** on `fix/guest_fix-tailing` (matches brief), diff vs `main` per `.manigot/manigot.json`.\n- **TASK-1 (capture verified + pinned):** `DockerInvocation.Run`'s `cmd.Stdout = stdout` wiring is correct — with a non-`*os.File` writer, exec.Cmd pipes and forwards every chunk. Three new `docker_test.go` tests pin byte-exact capture (incl. non-zero exit, missing trailing newline); the opencode JSONL marker test now asserts raw JSONL lands verbatim in `session.log`. The job's own `session.log` artifact confirms the full raw opencode JSONL stream is captured verbatim with per-event timestamps.\n- **TASK-2 (live streaming):** `openSessionLog` (header before invocation) + `sessionLog` writer (trailing-newline guarantee) + `ensureSessionLogFile` (run-start creation); `AgentRunner.Run` takes a `live` writer, tee'd via `io.MultiWriter`; the Run loop opens before/closes after each invocation with `io.Discard` degradation; sweep ordering (per-invocation commits the section, loop-exit sweep backstops) is correct and pinned by `TestRunWritesSessionLogPerInvocation` (linked worktree + clean-tree assertion) and the header-before test.\n- **TASK-3 (TUI):** \"l\" now tails `<job.Dir>/session.log` gated on `sessionLogExists`; log tab (key 5) stays on `run.log` — the log-vs-tail distinction is real; all three tail tests updated.\n- **TASK-4 (docs):** AGENTS.md, README.md, project-template, ROADMAP updated; stale `appendSessionLog` comment in entrypoint.sh synced. No out-of-scope changes.\n\n**Non-blocking notes recorded in the verdict:** (1) a mid-run session.log *write* failure would propagate through the MultiWriter and could abort the invocation (contrary to the best-effort intent that only covers open failures) — low-probability, not a blocker; (2) legacy jobs with only pre-fix run.log show the \"no run yet\" message on \"l\"; (3) the job's own uncommitted developer section in session.log is an interrupted-run artifact, not a code defect — tests prove a normal run leaves the tree clean, and the host sweep commits the remainder.","time":{"start":1787921802337,"end":1787921809274}}}
